From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: raphael1688 <schuey@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 07 Nov 2026 09:27:18 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Patch support Home Assistant ingress

Home Assistant can only show an add-on in its sidebar through ingress,
which serves the add-on under a per-install path prefix
(/api/hassio_ingress/<token>). The interface assumed it lives at the
root of its own port: it called its API at /api/..., loaded its images
and built files from /, and routed without a base path. Under ingress
/api/... even reaches Home Assistant's own API instead.

Make that prefix a runtime setting:

  - Vite builds with a relative base, so the built files and the lazily
    loaded pages load relative to the page.

  - index.html carries an empty ingress-path meta tag. The add-on's
    ingress server fills it in from the X-Ingress-Path header. On the
    admin port it stays empty and the interface behaves as before.

  - A small BasePath module reads that tag. The API client, the router
    basename and the image paths use it. So do the addresses of the
    menu and dashboard links, so that they also open in a new tab.

  - Because the files now load relative to the page, a page opened at a
    nested route asks for e.g. /nginx/assets/index.js. The admin
    interface's nginx configuration serves those from the top level.
---
